    "text": "Iohannes se godspellere, \u00fee \u00f0is godspell awrat, s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t se H\u00e6lend her on \u00feisum life on sumne s\u00e6l\nSe \u00fee me ne lufa\u00f0, ne hylt he mine spr\u00e6ce.\nAnd seo spr\u00e6c \u00fee ge gehyrdon, nis heo na min spr\u00e6c, ac \u00fe\u00e6s ylcan F\u00e6der \u00fee me asende.\nIc spr\u00e6c \u00f0as \u00feing to eow mid eow nu wunigende.\nSe halga Froforgast \u00fee min F\u00e6der asent on minum naman eow, he eow t\u00e6c\u00f0 ealle \u00feing, and eow ealle\nIc forl\u00e6te eow sibbe, and mine sibbe eow sylle.\nNe forgife ic eow swa swa \u00fees middaneard gif\u00f0.\nNe beo eower heorte gedrefed, ne ne forhtige nateshwon.\nGe gehyrdon \u00fe\u00e6t ic s\u00e6de so\u00f0lice nu eow, \u00fe\u00e6t ic sylf nu fare, and ic cume to eow.\nGif ge me lufedon, ge witodlice blissodon, for \u00f0am \u00fee ic fare to minum F\u00e6der nu, for \u00f0an \u00fee se F\u00e6der\nAnd nu ic hit eow secge \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee hit gewur\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t ge \u00feonne his gelyfon \u00feonne hit gedon bi\u00f0.\nNe sprece ic na fela \u00feing heonon for\u00f0 to eow.\n\u00d0ises middaneardes ealdor to me sylfum becom, and he nan \u00feing n\u00e6f\u00f0 eallunga on me; ac oncnawe \u00fees\nSe H\u00e6lend us s\u00e6de on \u00feisum halgan godspelle \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00f0e me lufa\u00f0, he hylt mine spr\u00e6ce.\n\u00de\u00e6re lufe fandung is \u00fe\u00e6s weorces fremming, \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00fe\u00e6t God wile \u00fea weorc habban \u00e6t us, \u00fe\u00e6t we mid\nAnd min F\u00e6der hine lufa\u00f0, and wit becuma\u00f0 to him, and mid him wunia\u00f0 witodlice begen.\nGes\u00e6lig bi\u00f0 se mann \u00fee swilce cuman underfeh\u00f0, gif he mid un\u00feeawum hi aweg ne adrif\u00f0, ne mid\nNe hi ne cuma\u00f0 na butan heora begra Lufu, \u00fe\u00e6t is se Halga Gast, \u00fee hi asendon begen on \u00feysum ylcan\nGod sylf afanda\u00f0 \u00e6lces mannes heortan, hw\u00e6\u00f0er se mann wylle his wununge habban, o\u00fe\u00fee leahtras\nSe H\u00e6lend us s\u00e6de on \u00feysum so\u00f0um godspelle, Se \u00f0e me ne lufa\u00f0, ne hylt he mine spr\u00e6ce.\nNe bi\u00f0 seo lufu idel, gif heo God lufa\u00f0, ac wyrc\u00f0 mihtilice micele \u00feing \u00e6fre, and gif heo wyrcan nele,\nGodes lufu sceal beon geswutelod on us on mu\u00f0e and on mode and on \u00fe\u00e6s mannes life, \u00fe\u00e6t he Godes\nAnd seo spr\u00e6c \u00fee ge gehyrdon, nis heo na min spr\u00e6c, ac \u00fe\u00e6s ylcan F\u00e6der \u00fee me asende.\nSe H\u00e6lend, \u00fee \u00f0is spr\u00e6c, is gehaten Word, of \u00f0am F\u00e6der acenned, and he sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0 for\u00f0i \u00fe\u00e6t seo\nIc spr\u00e6c \u00feas \u00f0ing to eow mid eow nu wunigende.\nHe w\u00e6s \u00f0a mid heom wunigende lichamlice, and he heom fram ferde swi\u00f0e fus to heofonum, to his\nSe halga Frofergast, \u00fee min F\u00e6der asent on minum naman eow, he eow t\u00e6c\u00f0 ealle \u00feing, and eow ealle\nSe Halga Gast is gehaten Paraclitus on Greciscre spr\u00e6ce, and on Leden Consolator, \u00fe\u00e6t is Frefrigend\nHe wear\u00f0 asend \u00fea, swa swa se H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de, fram \u00f0am halgan F\u00e6der, and fram his Suna eac, on fyres\nWe habba\u00f0 ges\u00e6d swutellicor be \u00feisum on \u00feam o\u00f0rum spelle \u00fee her to gebyra\u00f0, on \u00feam man m\u00e6g\nButon se Halga Gast nu eowre heortan onlihte mid his gastlican gife, ne ga\u00f0 ure word aht innto eowre\nEalle ge gehyra\u00f0 \u00feas ane r\u00e6dinge, and swa\u00f0eah butan twyn ne beo\u00f0 ealle eowre mod gelice onlihte\nSe H\u00e6lend \u00fea s\u00e6de his apostolum \u00feus: Ic forl\u00e6te eow sibbe, and mine sibbe eow sylle.\nSibbe he forgeaf symle his apostolum, and sibbe he lufa\u00f0 on geleaffullum mannum, mid so\u00f0f\u00e6stnysse,\nHe forlet hi on sibbe, and heom sy\u00f0\u00f0an forgeaf his \u00fea ecan sibbe on his rice mid him.\nNe forgife ic eow swa swa \u00f0es middaneard forgif\u00f0.\n\u00d0es middaneard forgif\u00f0 \u00fea gewitendlican \u00feing, and he forgif\u00f0 \u00fea ecan \u00feam \u00fee hine lufia\u00f0.\nNe beo eower heorte gedrefed, ne ne forhtige nateshwon.\nSe H\u00e6lend hi gefrefrode mid his f\u00e6gerum wordum, nolde \u00fe\u00e6t hi wurdon wi\u00f0innan gedrefede for his\nFor \u00f0an \u00fee he \u00f0a ferde, and he gefette hi eft to \u00fe\u00e6re ecan blisse, swa swa he heom behet.\nGif ge me lufedon, ge witodlice blissodon, for \u00f0an \u00fee ic fare to minum F\u00e6der nu, for \u00f0an \u00fee se F\u00e6der\nHi lufodon hine ealle, and swa\u00f0eah forhtodon, for \u00f0an \u00fee he swa fus w\u00e6s fram heom \u00fea to heofonum,\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re menniscnysse is se F\u00e6der mare, and be \u00fe\u00e6re he spr\u00e6c swa \u00e6r his \u00f0rowunge, \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee he\nBe \u00feam \u00f0e he so\u00f0 God is, he w\u00e6s symle acenned of \u00f0am \u00e6lmihtigan F\u00e6der, eal swa mihtig swa he,\nArrius hatte iu sum healic gedwola, se wolde lytlian \u00feone leofan H\u00e6lend, \u00fe\u00e6t he unmihtigre w\u00e6re on\nOlimpius w\u00e6s gehaten sum o\u00f0er gedwola, se s\u00e6t him on b\u00e6\u00f0e, and he unges\u00e6liglice spr\u00e6c mid\nWe sceolon gelyfan on \u00feone lyfigendan H\u00e6lend, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6lmihtig God is \u00e6fre mid \u00feam F\u00e6der, and\n\u00d0is godspell seg\u00f0 git for\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t se H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de \u00f0a, And nu ic hit eow secge \u00e6r \u00f0an \u00fee hit gewur\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00deis is swutellice ges\u00e6d, and he s\u00e6de for\u00f0 git, Ne sprece ic na fela \u00feing heonon for\u00f0 to eow, for \u00f0an \u00fee\n\u00d0ises middaneardes ealdor to me sylfum becom, and he nan \u00f0ing n\u00e6f\u00f0 eallunga on me.\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6s se sylfa deofol, \u00fee on \u00f0am synfullum rixa\u00f0, and is yfel ealdor arleasra manna, se com to \u00feam\nSe deofol \u00fea forleas \u00fe\u00e6t he gel\u00e6ht h\u00e6fde to his anwealde \u00e6ror of Adames cynne, eall \u00fe\u00e6t on God\nSe h\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea gyt on \u00feises godspelles ende, Ac oncnawe \u00fees middaneard \u00fe\u00e6t ic minne F\u00e6der\nOn \u00feam we magon tocnawan \u00fe\u00e6t Crist lufode his F\u00e6der, on \u00feam \u00fee he w\u00e6s gehyrsum his F\u00e6der o\u00fe",
